# UI Design Strategy Guide

The web UI is at `/app/` (namespace `app`). The classic UI (`/minimal/`, Bootstrap and jQuery)
was removed on 2026-10-15. Do not add it back.

## 1. Folder and file structure
- **Views:** `budgetapp/app/views/`, 1 file per feature. Class-based views only.
- **Money logic:** `budgetapp/services/`. Every month figure comes from
  `build_month_snapshot()` in `budgetapp/services/month.py`.
- **Templates:** pages in `templates/app/`, reusable parts in `templates/app/components/`,
  HTMX fragments in `templates/app/partials/`. The PDF report is `templates/app/pdf/`.
- **CSS:** `static/app/css/`: `tokens.css` (colors, spacing, dark mode), `components.css`,
  `pages.css`, `auth.css`. Use the tokens; do not write fixed colors.
- **JS:** `static/app/js/`. Third-party files are in `static/app/vendor/` (HTMX, anime.js).

## 2. Base template
- Every page extends `app/base.html`. Sign-in pages extend `account/base.html`.
- No inline `<script>` or `style=` in templates. Keep HTML, JS and CSS in separate files.

## 3. Libraries
- **HTMX** for server requests. A view answers with a partial and an `HX-Trigger` event
  (for example `monthChanged`, `goalsChanged`) so other parts refresh.
- **anime.js** for animation. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Small vanilla JS for the rest (sheets, toasts, quick add, the offline outbox).

## 4. Patterns
- Edit forms open in the bottom sheet (`#edit-sheet`).
- Deletes use "tap again" (`data-confirm-tap`), not a confirm dialog.
- After a spend, show a toast with Undo.
- Every page works on a phone (16px side gutter) and in dark mode.
